# =============================================================================
# .kilocodeignore — ZeroAgent Studio
# =============================================================================
# Files Kilo Code must NOT load into context. Standard gitignore syntax.
#
# In Kilo v7 this file is the legacy mechanism; the modern equivalent is
# `permission.read` / `permission.edit` deny rules in `.kilo/kilo.jsonc`
# (see the `permission` block there). The IgnoreMigrator still reads this
# file and converts patterns into deny rules on `read` and `edit` tools, so
# keeping it in sync is defense-in-depth: the patterns apply even if
# kilo.jsonc is missing, misconfigured, or being read by a legacy extension.
#
# Mirror of `.cursorignore` for symmetry across coding agents. The two files
# MUST stay in sync — if you add a pattern here, add it there too (and to
# `.gitignore` if the path is also ephemeral on disk).
#
# IMPORTANT — track on purpose, do NOT add here:
#   .kilo/rules/**          Architecture & quality rules
#   .kilo/skills/**        Portable workflow skills
#   .kilo/agents/**        Specialized personas
#   .kilo/command/**       Slash commands
#
# Companion files:
#   .gitignore             What Git must not track
#   .cursorignore          Mirror for Cursor
#   .kilo/kilo.jsonc       Kilo config (permissions, agents, instructions)
# =============================================================================

